  "summary": "JSCeal is a cryptocurrency-focused stealer delivered as Brotli-compressed, javascript-obfuscator-protected V8 bytecode (.jsc) executed by a bundled Node.js runtime. It steals browser cookies and saved credentials, keylogs, captures screenshots, targets crypto wallets and Telegram/installed applications, and intercepts HTTPS locally through a MITM proxy with its own generated certificate. The payload is launched by a PowerShell stage via node.exe -r preflight.js app.jsc, which decompresses and loads the malware.",
  "mitre_techniques": [
    "T1056.001",
    "T1113",
    "T1539",
    "T1555.003",
    "T1557",
    "T1059.001"
  ],
